Assembler Version 13
====================
Assembled by: version 12 (both instgen and asm)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
All features from version 12, plus one new instruction:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n and \\ escapes
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment (including label refs)
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx (with zero-fill on pass 2)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels
- Relative branch labels (auto-detected via instruction flags)
- Labels as 2-byte operands
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- Flag-based operand type detection
- .include directive for including external files
- .zeropage and .code section directives
- Command-line arguments: <assembler> <input> <output>

Directives:
- .include filename
- .zeropage - switches to zero page section
- .code - switches back to code section

Instruction set: same as version 12, plus:
- ASLZ (arithmetic shift left, zero page - opcode $06)

Error handling: same as version 12 (errors 1-D)

New in this version (relative to version 12):
- New instruction: ASLZ (zero page arithmetic shift left)
- Major internal refactoring into separate modules (no new external features)
- Source split into: asm.asm, common.asm, hash_table.asm, file_stack.asm,
  to_decimal.asm, environment.asm
- Parameterized hash table: common.asm defines HT_KEY, HT_VL, HT_VH before
  including hash_table.asm, allowing the hash table to be reused with
  different key/value bindings
- Parameterized file stack: FS_FILENAME, FS_CURR_FILE, FS_CURR_LINEL,
  FS_CURR_LINEH defined before including file_stack.asm
- Hash table uses split low/high access via single pointer HTPL/HTPH
  (HASH at offset 0 for low byte, HASH+$80 for high byte) instead of
  separate HTLPL/HTHPL pointers from version 12
- TOKEN buffer moved to absolute address $1E00 (from zero page at $24)
- TOKEN2 buffer at $1D00
- LHASHTAB at $1F00 (single 256-byte region)
- Hash table variables allocated via .zeropage DATA $00 instead of explicit
  = assignments
- Hash table stores value together with token in store_token (value stored
  inline after token name on heap)

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
- Non-standard mnemonic syntax (LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, BITZ, INCZ, etc.)
- DATA pseudo-instruction
- DATA $00 for zero page variable allocation in .zeropage section
- Hex constants ($xx and $xxxx)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Labels and label assignments (label = value)
- PC setting (* = $2000 and * = $FFFC for vectors)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Labels as absolute 2-byte operands
- Comments (;)
- BRK with inline error code and message
- .include directive (out/inst.asm.out, environment.asm, common.asm,
  file_stack.asm, to_decimal.asm)
- .zeropage and .code section directives
- Command-line arg access: argc, argv
- File I/O: open, close, read, openout, write

New syntax used in source (relative to version 12):
- .zeropage and .code section directives (replaces explicit = assignments
  for zero page variables)

Other source changes:
- Modular source structure: hash_table.asm, file_stack.asm, to_decimal.asm
  extracted as reusable modules
- Parameterized includes: HT_KEY = TOKEN, HT_VL = HEX2, HT_VH = HEX1
  defined before .include hash_table.asm; FS_FILENAME = TOKEN, etc. defined
  before .include file_stack.asm
- TOKEN moved from zero page to absolute address $1E00
- instgen.asm also uses .zeropage/.code and parameterized common.asm
